\subsection{Ejercicio 23: caudal en una tubería}
Con $R=0.25$ in y $v(r)=80(1-r/R)^{1/7}$:
\[Q=\int_0^{0.25}160\pi r(1-4r)^{1/7}\,dr,\qquad h=0.03125,\ n=8.\]
\begin{table}[H]\centering\caption{Nodos de $f(r)=160\pi r(1-4r)^{1/7}$}\small\begin{tabular}{rrr|rrr}\toprule $i$&$r_i$&$f_i$&$i$&$x_i$&$f_i$\\\midrule
0 & 0.00000 & 0.000000 & 5 & 0.15625 & 68.271148\\
1 & 0.03125 & 15.411159 & 6 & 0.18750 & 77.314786\\
2 & 0.06250 & 30.150983 & 7 & 0.21875 & 81.696803\\
3 & 0.09375 & 44.063717 & 8 & 0.25000 & 0.000000\\
4 & 0.12500 & 56.908296 &  &  & \\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}\end{table}
\begin{align*}
T&=\tfrac{0.03125}{2}[f_0+f_8+2(f_1+f_2+f_3+f_4+f_5+f_6+f_7)]\\
 &=\boxed{11.681778\ \mathrm{in}^3/\mathrm{s}},\\
S_{1/3}&=\tfrac{0.03125}{3}[f_0+f_8+4(f_1+f_3+f_5+f_7)+2(f_2+f_4+f_6)]\\
 &=\boxed{12.151244\ \mathrm{in}^3/\mathrm{s}}.
\end{align*}
Con $u=r/R$, la integral exacta es:
\begin{align*}
Q&=160\pi R^2\int_0^1u(1-u)^{1/7}\,du\\
